## Printed
heading: FUN'S
heading: CROSS WORD PUZZLE
number: No 26
heading: Can You Solve It?
intro: Today's cross-word puzzle, the twenty-sixth in FUN'S series, is contributed by Charles L. Rives of Spring Valley, N. Y. Mr. Rives writes that he has found it easier to solve one of these puzzles than to originate one and he wonders how many of FUN'S readers will succeed in solving his puzzle. Fill in the small squares with words coresponding to the list of clews and definitions given below, allowing one letter to each square. The solution to this puzzle will be given in next week's FUN.
solution heading: SOLUTION TO X-WORD PUZZLE No 26


